@startuml
'===============================================================
' PegaIndexWorkspaceProcess — Target Design (NEW)
' 1. DataPage D_LatestRules4ExactedApps → initial rule list
' 2. Schema-driven relative discovery via backend
' 3. Recursive queue with dedup
'===============================================================

title Pega Index Workspace Process\n(Target Design — DataPage + Schema-Driven Discovery)

|Extension|
start

:User triggers "Index Workspace";

== Phase 0: Project Detection ==

:Read **pega-project.json** from workspace root;
:Extract appName, operatorId;
:Compute projectId =\nSHA256("pega:" + appName).slice(0,12);
:Call **setProjectId(projectId)**;

== Phase 1: Initial Rule Enumeration (DataPage — App-Centric) ==

|Pega Server|
:POST **D_LatestRules4ExactedApps**\n  Body: { "ApplicationNames": "{appName}" };
note right
  DataPage returns ALL latest rules
  belonging to this Application stack.
  Single API call — no per-RuleSet pagination.
  Returns: { pxResults: RuleSummary[] }
end note

|Extension|
:Receive **RuleSummaryList** (pxResults);
:Create **dedupSet** = Set<string>\n(key = "{pxObjClass}!{pyClassName}!{pyRuleName}");
:Create **fetchQueue** = Queue(RuleSummaryList);
:Add all items to dedupSet;

== Phase 2: Fetch + Schema-Driven Relative Discovery ==

:Call **calibrateFetchConcurrency()**;

repeat
  :Pick next batch from **fetchQueue** (chunk=50);

  |Pega Server|
  :Fetch rule content in parallel\nvia GET /rules/{pzInsKey};

  |Extension|
  :For each fetched rule:;
  :Save to disk:\n**./rules/{appliedClass}/{pyRuleName}.pega.json**;

  :Send rule to Backend for ingest;

  |Backend Server|
  :POST **/api/v1/pega/ingest-rule**\nBody: { projectId, ruleJson };

  :1. **ingestRule()** → KB + Graph;

  :2. **extractRelatives(ruleJson)**:;
  note right
    a. Lookup pxObjClass in pega-core-schemas.json
    b. Get schema.dependencyPaths[]
    c. Traverse each path in ruleJson
    d. Extract referenced rule identifiers
    e. Resolve to { pxObjClass, pyClassName, pyRuleName, insKey }
  end note

  :Return **RelativeRuleInfoList[]**;

  |Extension|
  :For each relative in RelativeRuleInfoList:;

  if (dedupSet.contains(\n{objClass}!{className}!{ruleName})) then (already known)
    :Skip;
  else (new rule discovered)
    :dedupSet.add(key);
    :fetchQueue.enqueue(relative);
  endif

repeat while (fetchQueue.isEmpty()?) is (no)

:All rules fetched + all schema-driven relatives discovered;

== Phase 3: Finalize ==

|Backend Server|
:queryPegaTotals() → compute DB stats;

|Extension|
:Report: "🏛️ Pega: Ingested {N} rules\n(initial: {I} from DataPage,\ndiscovered: {D} via schema relations)";

stop

== Key Design Decisions ==

note as DesignNotes
**1. DataPage vs per-RuleSet enumeration:**
  DataPage D_LatestRules4ExactedApps = 1 API call
  → trả latest version only
  → app-centric (tất cả rules thuộc app stack)
  → không cần resolve hierarchy/rulesets trước

**2. Schema-driven relative discovery:**
  Backend dùng pega-core-schemas.json → dependencyPaths
  → chỉ fetch rules thực sự được reference
  → không blind expand 9 types cho mọi class

**3. Per-rule ingest (not batch NDJSON):**
  Mỗi rule ingest ngay → backend trả relatives ngay
  → Extension queue relatives → fetch tiếp
  → Recursive BFS cho tới khi queue empty

**4. Dedup key:**
  "{pxObjClass}!{pyClassName}!{pyRuleName}"
  → check TRƯỚC fetch → save bandwidth
end note

@enduml
